-- title:
--   Cotangent module of a p-divisible group is free of rank n
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative noetherian ring, let $I\subseteq R$ be an ideal for which $R$ is $I$-adically complete (and separated), let $p,h$ be natural numbers with the image of $p$ in $R$ lying in $I$, and let $G$ be a $p$-divisible group of height $h$ over $R$ in the sense of the structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): a family of levels $G.\mathrm{level}\,v$, each a commutative ring carrying a cocommutative Hopf $R$-algebra structure which is finite and free as an $R$-module of rank $p^{vh}$, together with surjective coalgebra-algebra maps $G.\mathrm{transition}\,v\colon G.\mathrm{level}(v+1)\to G.\mathrm{level}\,v$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^{v}$. Write $\mathrm{Cotangent}\,v$ for the cotangent module $I_v/I_v^2$ of the augmentation ideal $I_v$ of level $v$, and $\mathrm{cotangentMap}\,v$ for the map $\mathrm{Cotangent}(v+1)\to\mathrm{Cotangent}\,v$ induced by the transition map. Assume $G$ has dimension $n$, i.e. for every $v$ there exists some $R$-linear isomorphism $\mathrm{Cotangent}\,v\cong (R/(p^{v}))^{n}$, with no compatibility in $v$ required. Then the module $G.\mathrm{cotangentModule}$ of sequences $(x_v)$ with $\mathrm{cotangentMap}\,v\,(x_{v+1})=x_v$ admits an $R$-basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$; each projection $\mathrm{cotangentModuleProj}\,v$ to $\mathrm{Cotangent}\,v$ is surjective; and its kernel is $p^{v}$ times the whole module.
--
--   This is Tate's description of the module of invariant differentials $\omega_G=\varprojlim_v\omega_{G_v}$ of a $p$-divisible group of dimension $n$ over a complete noetherian base: it is free of rank $n$ and recovers each level cotangent space as $\omega_G/p^{v}\omega_G$, so that compatibility of the abstract level-by-level isomorphisms is automatic. It feeds the Cartier-duality results on the Tate module of $G$ over the ring of integers of a $p$-adic field, in particular the construction of invariant functionals and the linear independence statements used there.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_nonempty_basis_cotangentModule_of_hasDimension.lean

import Mathlib
